            <ArticleTitle>Asthma-how does it impact academic achievement and school budgets?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>202-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are many more students with asthma attending public schools than previously known and documented. The challenge to identify and educate students remains largely with local school districts. A student's academic success is impacted by thorough planning and provision for the student's needs. Collecting and measuring asthma-related absence data can help drive program planning and impact school budgets.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
